{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012497-homebrew-silent-hill-mystery","id":1012497,"title":"[Homebrew] Silent Hill Mystery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-05T04:59:16-08:00","id":1012497,"title":"[Homebrew] Silent Hill Mystery","content":"So I ran a one shot based on Silent Hill and used that.<br /> <br /> <b>Silent Hill\u2019s Mystery</b><br /> The town of Silent Hill present Irises to an alternate dimension that doesn\u2019t fit in the cosmology ie it\u2019s not the Shadow, the Astral or the Underworld. Some of these Irises are visible to Sleepers (fortunately they open only at auspicious times), others to being with Unseen Senses, and others to Mages with Mind or Space Mage Sight. Yes that means that Mastigo\u00ef makes one third of Silent Hill\u2019s Awakened because so many are attracted to the Mystery.<br /> <br /> Irises leads the traveler to a copy of the town with two visible characteristics: It\u2019s covered in thick white mist nearly blinding the traveler. And the distances seem warped: Places are closer than they should be. That last trait makes the City of Mists a practical but dangerous means of fast-travel from a point to another.<br /> <br /> Exiting the City of Mists is rather easy in theory. An Adept of Space can open a portal to return to reality and Irises leading to the material plane are plentiful. In general though the Iris you used to enter closes behind you.<br /> <br /> The Mist is a series of highly occulted Mysteries but some secrets can be gleaned in scrutinizing it by Mage Sight:<br /> <br /> 1 The Mist is animated if not alive.<br /> <br /> 2 The Mist probes the mind of those who travel in it. It\u2019s an effect that can be resisted with Mind Shield or Attainments that replicate it. Mages feel the probing.<br /> <br /> 3 The less Integrity (or equivalent) you have, the more difficult it is to resist the probing and the more chances the Mist take an interest in you.<br /> <br /> 4 Following some poorly understood conditions, (but very often linked to regrets, Derangements, or crimes), the Mist select a traveler or a group of travelers for an Ordeal, a potentially fatal journey of self-discovery<br /> <br /> 5 During an Ordeal, parts of the victim\u2019s soulscape are incorporated to the city\u2019s topography. If they die during their judgment these sceneries will remain, offering a grim reminder of whatever passion play occurred. That makes the City of Mists deeply incoherent to thorough explorers.<br /> <br /> 6 Sometimes if people die during the Ordeal they linger here without joining the Underworld. Sometimes they\u2019re changed in monsters to try others. Most of the time nobody has an idea of what happens to their souls.<br /> <br /> <b>Thoughts? I have more on the Ordeal itself but I have not used it yet. Other versions of what Silent Hill could be like in a Nmage setting?</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T05:08:10-08:00","id":1012499,"title":"","content":"This looks really interesting x3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T05:12:03-08:00","id":1012501,"title":"","content":"Having no knowledge of Silent Hill, I find the mystery intriguing. I presume Silent Hill is a small town? If so, then it would likely have an abnormally large number of mages in it given it has a mystery similar in scope (or at least I think it is) to the ones presented in the core book.<br /> <br /> Overall? I'd play in that Mage game. Granted I'm biased since I find Mastagos mysteries interesting, but yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T05:16:50-08:00","id":1012506,"title":"","content":"A cool idea for an Emanation Realm from Pandemonium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T05:40:44-08:00","id":1012519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012497-homebrew-silent-hill-mystery?p=1012501#post1012501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having no knowledge of Silent Hill, I find the mystery intriguing. I presume Silent Hill is a small town? If so, then it would likely have an abnormally large number of mages in it given it has a mystery similar in scope (or at least I think it is) to the ones presented in the core book.<br /> <br /> Overall? I'd play in that Mage game. Granted I'm biased since I find Mastagos mysteries interesting, but yeah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes Silent Hill has an Awakened population well above what a small town should have because of the Mystery. it happens sometimes. The largest Consilium in England is by instance in the South East because Merlin, it's pointedly not London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T09:11:23-08:00","id":1012617,"title":"","content":"From what I remember Silent Hill as a place (at least in Silent Hill 2, widely regarded as The Best Silent Hill Game) exists to force people to face and come to terms with things they deny about themselves, especially relating to parts of themselves they're ashamed of or horrible things they've done.<br /> <br /> I feel like Silent Hill would work really well as a Verge leading to a Pandemonic Emanation Realm of Guilt/Shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T09:29:32-08:00","id":1012622,"title":"","content":"I've shown this to my friend and they got inspired even though they didn't play any Silent Hill games. This is a sign that write up is good, clear and understands what it wants to do. Kudos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T17:01:14-08:00","id":1015900,"title":"","content":"This is very inspirational. Thank you for sharing it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T12:03:24-07:00","id":1098832,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/799082-cofd-diy-mystery-cults?p=1048455#post1048455\">Bound to the Town</a> from this linked post is a version I updated from the the <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/fansups.html\" target=\"_blank\">Silent Hill fanbook</a>. Linking it to a mystery cult seemed perfect. Like how you frame it in Mage terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 05-31-2017, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}